# Launch profile of the speculative configuration (RadixArk DFlash2, K = 7, --max-num-seqs 128). Source it AFTER env/host.env
# and ONLY for speculative launches: it is not part of host.env on purpose (host.env is sourced by every launch, the non-speculative
# --max-num-seqs 256 launch included, whose 384..511-token prefill batches would then move onto the sequence-parallel stream
# without anybody having measured them).
#
# Why: a verify batch has 8 tokens per request. With the default capture list (graphs up to 512 tokens) the verify batches of 33..64
# requests (264..512 tokens) either replay a graph or run on the replicated stream, with the pooler / unpooler GEMMs computed on
# every rank (8x the FLOPs, ~100-120 us per call at 512 rows). The vLLM branch keeps the sequence-parallel (SP) stream off every
# batch the graph dispatcher can serve: the floor is max(MIN_TOKENS, 257, largest capture size + 1), so with graphs up to 512 tokens
# the floor is 513 whatever MIN_TOKENS says (an env value below 513 is silently raised). Capturing graphs only up to 256 tokens and
# lowering the floor to 384 shards the stream from 48 requests (T = 384) on; those batches run eagerly (T > 256).
# S1-9 lever 1 A/B (2 sessions per arm, real prompts, exact KV bytes 9,676,390,400): real 512-token outputs c48 +3.6 %, c64 +5.7 %
# (the SP effect alone +4.3 % / +6.5 %, the eager tax -0.6 % / -0.8 %), 128-token mix rows c48 / c64 +0.4 / +1.4 % greedy,
# c16 / c32 / c128 flat within +-1.3 %. Details: docs/s19_spec_launch.md.
#
# The two settings are ONE launch property and must travel together:
#   - MIN_TOKENS=384 alone changes nothing (floor stays 513): the run is the old configuration;
#   - --max-cudagraph-capture-size 256 alone (env unset) gives the floor max(512, 257, 257) = 512 (A/B arm B512): 257..511-token
#     batches run eagerly and replicated, SP starts at 512 (c64 only), and NVML min free was 340 / 624 MiB against 920 / 772 MiB with
#     floor 384 and 400 / 484 MiB on the default list. Do not use it. Raising the env above the cap (MIN_TOKENS=520, arm B520:
#     257..519 eager and replicated) is the control that reached NVML min free 116 / 30 MiB (no OOM, no margin).
# After every boot run scripts/check_spec_launch.sh <serve.log>: it fails unless the log shows floor 384 and graphs up to 256.
#
# Usage (harness serve_sd.sh; SERVE_EXTRA carries the capture flag and the KV bytes of this profile):
#   source $HOST_DIR/env/host.env; source $HOST_DIR/env/spec_k7.env
#   SERVE_EXTRA="$MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS --kv-cache-memory-bytes $MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES" SPEC_CONFIG=dflash2_radixark ... serve_sd.sh <tag> ...
# or for a plain `vllm serve` line: vllm serve ... --speculative-config '<json>' $MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS --kv-cache-memory-bytes $MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES
#
# KV bytes (MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES, below): the exact --kv-cache-memory-bytes of this configuration, re-derived with the S1-7 procedure for this graph set. The graph pool
# shrinks from 2.11 to 1.22 GiB per rank (idle memory -912 MiB), so the S1-7 value 9,676,390,400 of the default capture list leaves S_live 2,167 MiB here (floor 1,256 MiB);
# 10,526,351,360 (513,982 blocks = 1,482,225 KV tokens, +8.8 %) leaves S_live 1,356.6 MiB, clean over the S1-7 stress (REPS = 2) and the GSM8K / determinism gates.
# Valid without prompt_logprobs / echo (S1-7 section 4). It belongs to this profile only: with the default capture list use 9,676,390,400. Re-derive it after any change
# of the sampler, the verify path, the graph set or max-num-batched-tokens (S1-7). The NVML min free of a boot is not the gate (it varies with the allocator cache).
#
# A preset value is kept (":=", as host.env does), e.g. VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS=520 plus the capture flag
# is the eager, replicated control of the A/B; scripts/check_spec_launch.sh takes the expected floor as its second argument.
: "${VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS:=384}"
export VLLM_MUSE_SPARK_SM120_SEQUENCE_PARALLEL_MIN_TOKENS
MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS="--max-cudagraph-capture-size 256"
export MUSE_SPEC_SERVE_ARGS
MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES=10526351360
export MUSE_SPEC_KV_BYTES
